  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14200385/assets/30e2b42fd5b3ab5fb1ee538079b518fa4b98a637e81d7f9aad23b4dd718a4541.png)\n\nThe graph $y={h}^{′}(x)$, the derivative of $y=h(x)$, is shown above. Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nI. $h(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-2$\n\nII. The graph of $y=h(x)$ is concave down on the interval $(-2,1)$\n\nIII. $h(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=3$",
